{"title":"Willow Physio","sub":"One appointment in seven is a no-show","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Healthcare services","geo":"Australia","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Capacity utilisation · no-shows · option comparison","prompt":"Willow runs 40 physiotherapists across Sydney, each with 16 half-hour appointments a day, 250 days a year, at $90 an appointment. About 15% of patients don't turn up and don't cancel. The CEO asks how much no-shows cost and what to do about them.","clarify":[{"q":"Reminders?","a":"None today. In a trial, an SMS reminder the day before cut no-shows to 9%. Each SMS costs about $0.10."},{"q":"Deposits?","a":"Taking a card deposit at booking cut no-shows to 5% in another clinic group, but about 5% of patients chose not to book at all."},{"q":"Overbooking?","a":"Some clinics book one extra patient a day per therapist, expecting at least one no-show."},{"q":"Waiting list?","a":"Most clinics have a short waiting list that can fill the odd late cancellation, but it could not replace a lasting fall in bookings."}],"structure":{"root":"How should Willow reduce the cost of no-shows?","branches":[{"head":"Size the problem","items":["Appointments × no-show rate × fee"]},{"head":"Options","items":["Reminders","Deposits","Overbooking"]},{"head":"Patient experience","items":["Fairness","Waiting times"]}]},"hypothesis":"No-shows waste a fixed cost: the physio is paid anyway. Reminders are cheap; deposits work but may put patients off.","questions":[{"q":"How much do no-shows cost Willow?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Appointments: 40 × 16 × 250 = 160,000. No-shows: 15% = 24,000. Lost revenue: <b>$2.16M a year</b>, and the physios are paid anyway.</p>"},{"q":"Compare reminders and deposits.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"396.308281pt\" height=\"159.66pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 396.308281 159.66\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style ty