L 43.148281 11.792 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 43.148281 133.76 L 389.108281 133.76 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(120.47652 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" d=\"M 3187 4467 L 3187 3994 L 1229 3994 L 1101 2291 L 1146 2291 Q 1254 2445 1376 2553 Q 1498 2662 1664 2723 Q 1830 2784 2061 2784 Q 2445 2784 2745 2617 Q 3046 2451 3219 2144 Q 3392 1837 3392 1402 Q 3392 966 3213 633 Q 3034 301 2698 112 Q 2362 -77 1888 -77 Q 1517 -77 1254 35 Q 992 147 809 320 Q 627 493 493 685 L 896 992 Q 1069 730 1277 566 Q 1485 403 1888 403 Q 2342 403 2582 646 Q 2822 890 2822 1331 L 2822 1395 Q 2822 1837 2582 2080 Q 2342 2323 1888 2323 Q 1581 2323 1405 2211 Q 1229 2099 1088 1946 L 634 2010 L 794 4467 L 3187 4467 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(295.203793 27.699294) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" d=\"M 1696 0 L 1120 0 L 2829 4006 L 922 4006 L 922 3174 L 442 3174 L 442 4467 L 3373 4467 L 3373 3994 L 1696 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p35bfa09ec1\"><rect x=\"43.148281\" y=\"11.792\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Extra revenue a year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>SMS reminders:</b> no-shows fall to 9%: 9,600 more appointments × $90 = $0.86M, less SMS costs $0.02M: <b>+$0.85M</b>.</p> <p><b>Deposits:</b> 5% fewer bookings, but only 5% no-shows: attended appointments = 95% × 95% = 90.25% of today's slots, against 85% now: <b>+$0.76M</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> reminders gain more, cost almost nothing and don't put patients off.</p>"},{"q":"Should Willow also overbook?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>With reminders, about 9% still don't come, so a physio with 16 bookings expects about 1.4 no-shows a day. One extra booking a day would usually be seen in a no-show gap, adding up to about $0.8M a year. But on days when everyone turns up, a patient waits or the physio works late. Use it only for therapists and times with high no-show rates, and use the waiting list to fill late cancellations first.</p>"}],"reco":"No-shows cost Willow about $2.2M a year in lost revenue. Start with SMS reminders the day before: they cut no-shows from 15% to about 9% and add about $0.85M a year for almost no cost, more than deposits ($0.76M), which also put some patients off. Then fill late gaps from the waiting list, and overbook only where no-show rates stay high. Risk: overbooking can make patients wait. Next step: roll out reminders to all clinics this month.","great":["Sizes the problem in dollars","Compares options including their side effects","Counts lost bookings from deposits","Treats overbooking carefully"],"id":80,"slug":"willow-physio"}